course: dictionary
lesson: 13933
title: Lengthened: made longer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Lengthened is a past-tense form of the verb lengthen, which means to make something longer or to become longer. «The tailor lengthened the trousers for the tall boy.» The tailor made the trousers longer, so lengthened means made longer.
explain: Lengthened can also be about time. «The days lengthened as spring arrived.» The days got longer, with more daylight. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try "made longer" in the sentence in place of the hard word and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Lengthen has four forms: lengthen, lengthens, lengthened and lengthening. Lengthened is the form for something that has already happened. It can also work as an adjective, as in «lengthened shadows», which are shadows that have grown longer.
fact: Lengthen means to make something longer, or to become longer.
fact: «Lengthened» is the past tense of «lengthen», so it tells us something has already happened.
fact: «The days lengthened» in spring and summer because the Earth's tilt points our half of the world towards the Sun.
fact: «Lengthened shadows» are shadows that have grown longer.
fact: In maths, a lengthened side changes the perimeter and the area of a shape.
exercise: «The tailor lengthened the trousers for the tall boy.» What does lengthened mean here? | *Made longer | Painted bright blue | Folded neatly | Made shorter
exercise: Mia says, «The days lengthened in June.» What does lengthened describe? | Days became colder | Days were cancelled | *Days became longer
exercise: «The school lengthened its break.» Find and copy the word that means made longer. | *lengthened | school | break | its
test: «The shadows lengthened as the sun sank low.» What does lengthened mean here? | Turned red | Became shorter | *Became longer | Fell over
test: Which word is closest in meaning to lengthened? | Cooked | *Extended | Folded | Shortened
exam: «The lesson was lengthened by ten minutes, so the class stayed longer.» What does lengthened mean? | Cancelled | Made shorter | *Made longer | Moved to the garden
